  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichthys_ocellatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This extremely rarely imported species originates from Burma. The charming fish attains a length of only 2-3 cm. This is the only species of anabantoid fish whose way of reproduction is still unknown. The only other member of the genus, P. lineatus, is a bubblenest builder although the eggs look like the eggs of mouthbrooders.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichthys_ocellatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In the habitats of P. ocellatus appear heavy day-night changes of the water temperature. The species lives in muddy, shallow pools. By day water temperature rises easily up to 25-28°C, while during the night the temperature becomes as low as 15°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichthys_ocellatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The metabolism of the tiny fish is adapted to those changes. So one should try to imitate them (for example by switching off the heater along with the lamps), otherwise the fish will become very sensitive to various diseases in the long term.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichthys_ocellatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The surfaces of the eggs of P. ocellatus also have the very characteristic structures of eggs of mouthbrooding species (this is known from dissected specimens). But as long as no one has ever bred the species successfully in an aquarium nobody will know for sure how they do it.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichthys_ocellatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Parasphaerichthys: ancient Greek, means \"similar to Sphaerichthys\". Sphaerichthys is another genus of fish. ocellatus: means \"bears an ocellus\".</p>"
    }
  ],
